Huan Pang received his PhD degree from Nanjing University in 2011. He is now a distinguished professor at Yangzhou University and a Young Changjiang Scholar of the Ministry of Education in China. He is a senior member of the Chinese Chemical Society. He is the managing editor of EnergyChem, the editorial board member of FlatChem and Rare Metals, and the youth editorial board member of Nano Research, Nano Research Energy, eScience among other distinguished academic journals. He was recognized as a highly cited researcher in Cross-Field by Clarivate Analytics in 2020 and 2021. He has won "Best Editor Award 2021" for his professional excellence and outstanding contribution to Nano Research. His research area mainly focuses on metal-organic frameworks (MOFs) related materials.
Yusuke Yamauchi received his PhD degree from Waseda University in 2007. He then joined the National Institute of Materials Science (NIMS) to start his research group. After being granted the ARC Future Fellowship, in May 2016, he joined the University of Wollongong as a Professor. In 2018, he moved to the University of Queensland as a Professor and a senior group leader at the Australian Institute for Bioengineering and Nanotechnology (AIBN). Concurrently, he serves as an honorary group leader at NIMS and an ERATO Research Director at the JST-ERATO Yamauchi Materials Space-Technics. His expertise is in inorganic material nanoarchitectonics.
